From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 07:50:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: keep an existing WLFW registration on repeated
 announce

Reopening the QRTR MHI channels can cause the same WLFW service to be
announced again. If firmware retained its session, a second HOST_CAP
request may be rejected with QMI_ERR_INCOMPATIBLE_STATE.

Use the already-registered bit in the IND_REGISTER response, as
Qualcomm CNSS does. Skip the initial host-capability exchange when the
host still has a registered wiphy and is not recovering. Keep the
existing exchange for a fresh or resetting session.

On Xiaomi Pad 8 Pro, initial firmware start reported status 0 and warm
D0 rollback reported 0xd. The driver kept the warm registration and
reconnected without repeating the rejected HOST_CAP request.

Codex investigated the WLAN suspend and remove paths, wrote the change,
and validated it with an ARM64 module build and a controlled D0 rollback.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
index 2e52849..c3d457c 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
@@ -2707,7 +2707,10 @@ out:
 		   ab->qmi.num_radios);
 }
 
-static int ath12k_qmi_fw_ind_register_send(struct ath12k_base *ab)
+#define ATH12K_QMI_FW_ALREADY_REGISTERED BIT_ULL(0)
+
+static int ath12k_qmi_fw_ind_register_send(struct ath12k_base *ab,
+					   bool *already_registered)
 {
 	struct qmi_wlanfw_ind_register_req_msg_v01 *req;
 	struct qmi_wlanfw_ind_register_resp_msg_v01 *resp;
@@ -2770,6 +2773,9 @@ static int ath12k_qmi_fw_ind_register_send(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 		goto out;
 	}
 
+	*already_registered = resp->fw_status_valid &&
+			      (resp->fw_status & ATH12K_QMI_FW_ALREADY_REGISTERED);
+
 out:
 	kfree(resp);
 resp_out:
@@ -4343,16 +4349,25 @@ int ath12k_qmi_event_server_arrive(struct ath12k_qmi *qmi)
 {
 	struct ath12k_base *ab = qmi->ab, *block_ab;
 	struct ath12k_hw_group *ag = ab->ag;
+	bool already_registered;
 	int ret;
 
 	ath12k_qmi_phy_cap_send(ab);
 
-	ret = ath12k_qmi_fw_ind_register_send(ab);
+	ret = ath12k_qmi_fw_ind_register_send(ab, &already_registered);
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		ath12k_warn(ab, "qmi failed to send FW indication QMI:%d\n", ret);
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	/* QRTR can announce a service again without a WLAN firmware restart. */
+	if (already_registered &&
+	    test_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_QMI_FW_READY_COMPLETE, &ab->dev_flags) &&
+	    test_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_REGISTERED, &ab->dev_flags) &&
+	    !test_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH, &ab->dev_flags) &&
+	    !test_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_RECOVERY, &ab->dev_flags))
+		return 0;
+
 	spin_lock(&qmi->event_lock);
 
 	ath12k_qmi_set_event_block(qmi, true);
-- 
